{
    "_comment": [
        "novafurryxl.json plus one LoraLoader - the SDXL twin of",
        "flux2-klein-lora.json. Use it when a style preset names a lora:",
        "",
        "  [images.styles.my-look]",
        "  workflow = \"novafurryxl-lora.json\"",
        "  model = \"novaFurryXL_ilV120.safetensors\"",
        "  lora = \"Zaush_-_Art_Style_Illustrious.safetensors\"",
        "  lora_strength = 0.7",
        "",
        "imgstyles.py turns lora/lora_strength into the {LORA} and",
        "{LORA_STRENGTH} tokens below. Everything else - checkpoint,",
        "sampler, steps, cfg, geometry - comes from _defaults, so a preset",
        "only has to name what it changes. {LORA} has no default: this",
        "workflow needs one named, and the run fails loudly rather than",
        "quietly drawing without it.",
        "",
        "The LoRA loads into BOTH model and CLIP, unlike the Flux one:",
        "SDXL style LoRAs are usually trained with the text encoder, and",
        "a model-only load quietly drops half of what you installed.",
        "",
        "Everything else - tokens, the SDXL notes, why there is no {VAE} -",
        "is documented in novafurryxl.json.",
        "",
        "This key is ignored by ComfyUI - it is not a node."
    ],
    "_defaults": {
        "MODEL": "novaFurryXL_ilV120.safetensors",
        "STEPS": 28,
        "CFG": 5.0,
        "SAMPLER": "euler_ancestral",
        "SCHEDULER": "normal",
        "WIDTH": 1280,
        "HEIGHT": 800,
        "LORA_STRENGTH": 0.8
    },
    "1": {
        "inputs": {
            "ckpt_name": "{MODEL}"
        },
        "class_type": "CheckpointLoaderSimple",
        "_meta": {"title": "Load Checkpoint"}
    },
    "8": {
        "inputs": {
            "lora_name": "{LORA}",
            "strength_model": "{LORA_STRENGTH}",
            "strength_clip": "{LORA_STRENGTH}",
            "model": ["1", 0],
            "clip": ["1", 1]
        },
        "class_type": "LoraLoader",
        "_meta": {"title": "Load LoRA"}
    },
    "2": {
        "inputs": {
            "text": "{STYLE}{PROMPT}",
            "clip": ["8", 1]
        },
        "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
        "_meta": {"title": "CLIP Text Encode (Positive)"}
    },
    "3": {
        "inputs": {
            "text": "{NEGATIVE}, worst quality, low quality, bad quality, lowres, jpeg artifacts, bad anatomy, bad proportions, bad hands, extra digits, fewer digits, deformed, mutated, sketch, unfinished, simple background, monochrome, speech bubble",
            "clip": ["8", 1]
        },
        "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
        "_meta": {"title": "CLIP Text Encode (Negative)"}
    },
    "4": {
        "inputs": {
            "width": "{WIDTH}",
            "height": "{HEIGHT}",
            "batch_size": 1
        },
        "class_type": "EmptyLatentImage",
        "_meta": {"title": "Empty Latent"}
    },
    "5": {
        "inputs": {
            "seed": "{SEED}",
            "steps": "{STEPS}",
            "cfg": "{CFG}",
            "sampler_name": "{SAMPLER}",
            "scheduler": "{SCHEDULER}",
            "denoise": 1,
            "model": ["8", 0],
            "positive": ["2", 0],
            "negative": ["3", 0],
            "latent_image": ["4", 0]
        },
        "class_type": "KSampler",
        "_meta": {"title": "KSampler"}
    },
    "6": {
        "inputs": {
            "samples": ["5", 0],
            "vae": ["1", 2]
        },
        "class_type": "VAEDecode",
        "_meta": {"title": "VAE Decode"}
    },
    "7": {
        "inputs": {
            "filename_prefix": "llm64",
            "images": ["6", 0]
        },
        "class_type": "SaveImage",
        "_meta": {"title": "Save Image"}
    }
}
